2026-11-07 | Session 003 | Standalone closed lid, banner, and add-ons · alpha.3
Objective: Replace the Amphetamine backend, expand the illustrated README, and
  implement a reviewed user-script/add-on workflow. Full feature parity is the
  product target, tracked separately from current alpha completion.
Changes:
  - Generated a matching night-workstation banner using the existing mascot as
    reference; expanded README navigation, feature matrix, architecture and guides.
  - Removed the Amphetamine service. Added a temporary admin-authorized power
    guard with exclusive ownership, PID/start identity, sequence/nonce lease,
    verified sleep restoration, and explicit root-record recovery.
  - Added add-on import, in-app script/manifest editor, exact-version approval,
    manual and session start/end events, example packages and cancellation.
  - Added an unprivileged process-group runner with clean environment, timeout,
    bounded capture, and quit cleanup; scripts never run in the power guard.
  - Added closed-lid design, add-on guide, and published-feature parity inventory.
  - Advanced version metadata and changelog to 0.1.0-alpha.3.
Verification:
  - 17 core/extension tests passed, including heartbeat replay/nonce/expiry,
    changed-script/manifest fingerprints, traversal rejection, clean environment,
    timeout, cancellation, and bounded output.
  - Build/run --verify, native runtime smoke test, and ad-hoc signature passed.
  - Owner approved ending the existing Amphetamine session and local administrator
    prompts. Standalone guard activation and normal stop restored sleep correctly.
  - Simulated Vibesomnia process exit: independent guard restored sleep and exited.
  - Suspended the app while its PID remained alive: heartbeat expiry restored sleep
    in about 8.4 seconds. Resumed app detected guard loss and ended the session.
  - At the end of isolated guard tests, SleepDisabled=0 and no worker/record remained.
  - Later system checks found SleepDisabled=1 again without a Vibesomnia owner.
    Amphetamine was fully closed through its menu; the unowned flag persisted.
    Requested owner confirmation before resetting another utility's global state.
    No Vibesomnia worker or root recovery record was left by the tests.
  - Computer-use UI: examples installed unapproved, read-only diagnostic reviewed
    and run, in-app edit saved, prior approval invalidated and Run disabled.
  - Markdown local links and banner dimensions (2172x724) verified; diff check clean.
  - Graph lookup/coverage used for existing session lifecycle; changed/stale files
    were read directly before relying on their current behavior.
Limitations: Physical lid/charger tests and remote reconnection from another device
  remain unverified. Root-worker forced-failure recovery and production distribution
  need more testing. Full Amphetamine parity and full remote desktop are not done;
  see docs/PARITY.md. No Community/Pro split or public binary release.
Delivery: Feature branch feat/standalone-closed-lid; source version v0.1.0-alpha.3.

Repository review: Draft PR #1 opened through the existing personal GitHub login;
  the generic connector/local default account lacked access to this private repo.
  Push and pull-request CI jobs passed. Repository visibility was not changed.

2026-11-07 | Session 004 | Desktop discovery correction · alpha.4
Objective: Fix ChatGPT detection and activate closed-lid mode for the owner's
  physical lid and remote-access test.
Changes:
  - Product detection checks bundle names alongside IDs: a ChatGPT-named build
    using com.openai.codex is ChatGPT, not a separate Codex installation.
  - Discovery includes running bundle URLs, Launch Services and system/user
    Applications folders. Launch and app-lifetime controls use detected identity.
  - Added three regression tests, updated test guide and alpha.4 version metadata.
Verification:
  - Graph lookup, relationship trace and coverage checks completed; source read.
  - All 20 tests passed; build/run --verify and ad-hoc signature verification passed.
  - Live app status reports ChatGPT and Claude Desktop installed and running.
  - Previous unowned override had already cleared (SleepDisabled=0); no reset made.
  - Owner authorized closed-lid activation and approved the administrator prompt.
  - Verified active closedLid session, SleepDisabled=1, guard process present,
    native idle-system assertion, and no idle-display assertion.
Handoff: Left indefinite closed-lid session running with display sleep allowed for
  the requested test. Battery protection remains enabled. Physical lid cycling
  and remote reconnection are not claimed as passed pending owner observation.

2026-11-07 | Session 005 | Private DMG installer and first-run setup · alpha.5
Objective: Produce a ready-to-install DMG/pkg and first-run setup while keeping
  the repository private and preserving the owner's active closed-lid session.
Changes:
  - Added universal release bundle construction, macOS package wizard, versioned
    DMG and checksum, and a validator that inspects without installing.
  - Installer targets Applications without relocation; preinstall refuses a
    running app/guard or leftover recovery record. No power/network/login changes.
  - Added welcome, app detection, saved sleep preferences, and optional guided
    remote test. Owner-confirmed results are distinct from automated evidence.
  - Added setup replay in toolbar/Settings and an isolated, read-only setup preview.
  - Added optional Developer ID signing/notarization path and manual private
    Actions artifacts. No release publishing or visibility-changing permissions.
  - Updated version metadata, README, distribution guide, tests and roadmap.
Verification:
  - Graph discovery/trace and relevant file coverage checked; sources read.
  - All 23 Swift tests passed, including persisted preferences and corrupt fallback.
  - Universal release build passed; image checksum, package layout/choice XML,
    app/CLI versions, macOS 14 targets, all arm64/x86_64 slices, bundled signatures,
    license, welcome/conclusion resources and preinstall contents verified.
  - Preinstall rejected the active session with an end/recover-and-quit message.
  - Computer use checked four setup preview pages, detection of ChatGPT/Claude,
    preference toggles/back navigation, and disabled power actions in preview.
  - Installer introduction/license screens inspected without accepting terms or
    performing a privileged installation. Duplicate title prefix corrected.
  - Existing alpha.4 PID and closed-lid session start time remained unchanged.
    Normal build/run --verify and runtime smoke test were not used because they
    would stop the owner's active session; separate bundle/preview checks used.
Limitations: Local app is ad-hoc signed; pkg is unsigned and unnotarized. No valid
  Developer ID identity was available. Actual installation, signed/notarized job,
  first launch from Applications, Intel hardware and physical lid/remote tests
  remain acceptance work. Manual installer workflow must reach the default branch
  before normal workflow dispatch. Main and repository visibility were not changed.
Delivery: alpha.5 source on feat/standalone-closed-lid; local DMG with checksum.

